मय-समय पर इसम� �रव्यू\n करने क� आवश्यकता है, इस \nसंबंध म� हमारा �रव्यू\n अंडर कं � स ड्र े श न भी है । गु\nड प्रेिक्टस गाइडलाइन्स भी जार� होनी \nचा�हए, ता�क लोग उसको ज्यादा से ज्यादा समझ स क� । म� यह मानकर चलता हूं �क यह \nअच्छ� स्क�म है, इसका ज्यादा प्रचार-प्रसार होना चा�हए ता�क आने वाले �दन� म� इस तरह \nके इको-म ा कर् प्रोडक्टस के प्र�त लोग� का रुझान बढ़े । \n \nSHRI SANTOSH BAGRODIA: Sir, since the hon. Minister has just now mentioned \nthat he is willing to review the Scheme, I would like to know whether the hon. Minister \nwould give preference to products in their procurement and also fiscal incentives for \ntheir exports. Similarly, I would also like to know from the hon. Minister as to how does \nthe Steering Committee chose a product -category for Eco-Mark Certification and which \nare the product categories under consideration of the Steering Committee; and does it \noverlap the mandate given to the Technical Committee and the BIS? \n\n4       Oral Answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nSHRI NAMO NARAIN MEENA: Sir, as far as th is Scheme is concerned, I would \nlike to submit that this is a voluntary Scheme. It is not binding, not only in our country, \nbut also throughout the world. The Government does not give any incentive to any \nindustry or product. At the same time, we have only  a few countries which are giving \nincentives in tenders for preferential purchases. No direct incentive is being given.  \nSo far as the functions of the Steering Committee and the Technical Committee are \nconcerned, as I mentioned earlier, the functions of th e Steering Committee are to \nformulate strategies for promotion, future development and improvement of the \nScheme. Whereas, the functions of the Technical Committee are to see the item and \nproduct concerned from the technical point of view. \nSHRI C. PERUMAL: Sir, I would like to know from the hon. Minister whether there \nis any law for making it compulsory to have eco -mark on certain products. If so, the \ndetails of enforcement machinery for detecting and punishing the violators? \nSHRI NAMO NARAIN MEENA: Sir, al l types of companies approach the Steering \nCommittee for marketing/labelling their products as eco-friendly. And then it goes to the \nTechnical Committee, and finally it goes to the Bureau of Indian Research for giving \neco-mark. If any company approaches fo r Eco-Mark Certification, it will be considered \naccordingly. \nSHRI MATILAL SARKAR: Sir, thank you for allowing me to put a supplementary. \nSir, the use of khadi products is dwindling. But, it is a fact that khadi products are eco -\nfriendly. So, I would like t o know, through you, from the hon. Minister whether the \nGovernment will consider including khadi products under eco- friendly scheme. If so, \nthe details may be given. \nSHRI NAMO NARAIN MEENA: Sir, as I have mentioned earlier, this scheme is \nvoluntary and non- binding. The hon. Member wants to know whether the Government \nis considering or can consider to give some incentives to Khadi. No such proposal is \npending with us. \n \nडा0 (श्रीमती) नजमा ए0 हेपतुल्ला : म� ऑनरे बल �म�नस्टर से आ प के थ्रू\n पू\nछना चाहूंगी \n�क यह जो आपने इको-फ्र� ड ल � प्रोडक्टस के �लए 16 के ट े ग र � ज आइड��टफाई क� है, सबसे \nज्यादा पौल्यू\nशन पैक े िजंग मैट��रयल से होता है । तो गवनर्म�ट क� क्या स्क�म है �क \nपॉ�लथीन और प्लािस्टक के यूज को �डस्करेज �कया जाए । क्या आप कु छ ऎसे इंस��टव लोग� \nको या एन0जी0ओज़0 वगैरह को द� गे ता�क वे इसको �डस्करेज क र के पैक े िजंग म� इको-फ्र� ड ल � \nमैट��रयल का यू\nज ज्यादा होने लगे ।  \n \nश्री नमो नारायण मीणा : सर, प्रोडक्ट के ट े ग र � ज म� प � के ि ज ं ग मेट��रयल और प्लािस्टक \nप्रोडक्ट को इसम� �लया हुआ है । अभी तक �कसी भी कम्पनी ने इ स के �लए एप्लाई नह� \n�कया है, wood substitute, finished leather and paper इसम� �कया हुआ है \n। प्लािस्टक का जहां तक सवाल है, य�द इसका �मसयू\nज होता है तो �बल्कु ल ह्यूमन हैल्थ \nके �लए और पयार्वरण खराबी के �लए काफ� असर पड़ता है और खास क र के जहां टू �रस्ट \nप्लेसेज म� हाई एल्ट�ट्यूडस म� लोग जाते है और वहां इसको छोड़कर आते ह� तो इसका गलत \nअसर पड़ता है । कई स्टे ट म� इसको जगह-जगह पर बंद �कया हुआ है । इ स के �लए कानून \nबना हुआ है और कह�  \n\nOral Answers [30 AUG., 2007] to Questions       5 \n \nबैन �कया हुआ है । अगर कोई स्टे ट चाहती है तो इसको एक प�टर्कु लर स्थान पर बेन �कया \nजा सकता है । ले�कन साथ ह� साथ हमको यह भी दे खना पड़ता है �क प्लािस्टक के बहुत \nसारे यूज ह� और उसका जब तक कोई आल्टरने�टव नह� आ जाता, तो एक साथ सबको बंद \nकरना संभव नह� है । ले�कन म� इससे सहमत हूं �क फे ज़ मैनर म� इ स के बारे म� कदम \nउठाते रहना चा�हए और जहां-जहां भी इनसे पयार्वरण खराब होता है या और कोई बात होती \nहै तो इस पर बैन लगना चा�हए ।  \nVanishing brides and abandoned grooms abroad \n*242. MS. SUSHILA TIR IYA: Will the Minister of OVERSEAS INDIAN \nAFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that the number of cases of vanishing brides and abandoned \ngrooms abroad has increased in the recent past; \n(b) whether Government had formed a Committee in this regard; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \nTHE MINISTER OF OVERSEAS INDIAN AFFAIRS (SHRI VAYALAR RAVI): \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n(a) to (c) The Ministry was created in May 2004 and since then the problem of \ndesertion of Indian women by their overseas Indian husbands is being monitored. The \ncomplaints received regarding Indian women deserted/divorced by their overseas Indian \nhusbands for the last 3 years is as follows: \nYear 2005 — 19 \nYear 2006 — 65 \nYear 2007 (till August) — 89 \nComplaints are also received in Ministry of Women and Child Development, NCW \nand NHRC. Thus, precise data on the number of cases of vanishing brides and \nabandoned grooms abroad is not available. An inter -Ministerial Committee has been \nconstituted to study the prob lems arising in marriages with overseas Indians and to \nsuggest ways to address them. \nMS. SUSHILA TIRIYA: Sir, the Minister has given data from 2005 to 2007. The \ndivorce rate in overseas is increasing. No doubt, the cases of brides vanishing abroad, as \nwell as, within India are also increasing. There are foeticides, murders, dowry deaths, \netc. So, my question to the hon. Minister is: May I know whether the Government has \nset up any judicial forum or any counselling centres, in India, to provide legal assista nce \nin India to avoid excessive litigation expenses, and to provide them counselling?  \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: Sir, the Ministry has taken certain initiatives. One of the \ninitiatives is that the Ministry has constituted an inter -Ministerial Committee on the \nbasis of the National Commission for Women's report. The Committee includes the \nMinistry of External Affairs, the Ministry of Overseas Indian Affairs, the Ministry of \nHome Affairs, and the Ministry of Law. Besides, the State Governments, the \n\n6       Oral Answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nNational Commission for Women, and the Human Rights Commission are also \ninvolved. So, this is the constitution of Inter -Ministerial Committee. They have \nappointed a Task Force. The Task Force is examining one of the proposals  of appointing \nSpecial Prosecutors. In every State, there should be Special Prosecutors to argue the \ncases. We are also thinking»in terms of repatriation of the accused, who is abroad. \nThirdly, where there is a bilateral agreement, a clause can be inserted  so that civil \nproceedings could be taken up in other countries also. These three issues are already \nunder the consideration of the Task Force. We are very much concerned about the plight \nof the women abroad. So, we are taking all the steps, including that  of financial \nassistance, maybe, of a meagre amount of one thousand dollars. But that is given for \npreparation and everything. The NGOs and others are also involved in this. The situation \nhas changed very much today only after the Ministry had taken the initiative during the \nlast three years. They have sensitised the whole issue, and every embassy has been \nsensitised. So, we are well aware that the number is increasing everyday. There are a \nlarge number of cases. This figure which I have given here is only the number of \ncomplaints which we have received. Thousands of people are not complaining to me. \nThis is also a problem. So, Sir, definitely, this Ministry will take all the initiatives. We \nare taking preventive measures also. We are taking all the initiati ves to see that the \nwomen's interests are protected, and that the women are protected. We will protect them \nand see that they are not orphaned abroad. \nMS. SUSHILA TIRIYA: Sir, my second supplementary is this. The National \nCommission for Women is delaying d owry harassment cases and some are pending \nsince 1998. So, my point is, there are many cases pending in the National Commission \nfor Women which have come from women staying abroad also. And, Sir, it is observed \nthat, sometimes, the Ministry's response is very much delayed. And it becomes very \ndifficult for the National Commission for Women to seek queries, come to the point, \nand draw up a conclusion. \nSir, I would like to know from the hon. Minister whether he has kept this in mind \nand whether there is any p roposal to set up a time limit to deal with the queries of these \nkinds of cases. How many cases are pending with you? And, how many months will you \ntake to deal with the cases of this nature? \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: Sir, my Ministry is responding instantly. I m yself made \nhundreds of telephone calls to the Ambassadors and Consulate Generals. As you know, \nSir, America, Canada, New Zealand, Australia and England are the main five countries \nwhich are involved in this. And, to some extent the Gulf is also involved. W e are in \ntouch with them. We write letters to them. The National Commission for Women is \ndoing a good job. The Women and Child Welfare Ministry is also involved in this. That \nis why, a task force has been constituted by the Inter -Ministerial Committee for this \npurpose. Money was allotted last year and this year also. An amount of Rs. 3 crores has \nbeen provided for the assistance of women abroad. All these initiatives have been taken \nin collaboration with the Women's Commission and also the Ministry of Women  and \nChild Welfare. Sir, one of the major components of this process is the State \nGovernment. They are very important partners because when we write letters to the \nChief Ministers ...(Interruptions)... \n\nOral Answers [30 AUG, 2007] to Questions      7 \nMS. SUSHILA TIRIYA: Sir, I am asking about the National Commission, not about \nthe State Commissions. ...(Interruptions)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Please, let the hon. Minister proceed. \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: As soon as we receive complaints, I used to write to the \nChief Ministers saying that the complaints from the lady may be documented for the \npurpose of FIR. They have done this in some States. This is number one. \nSecondly, I want to say that we are in close touch with the Women's Commission. \nTheir report is with me. On th e basis of this report, an Inter -Ministerial Committee has \nbeen formed. We are discussing it. We are having discussions with them also. There is \nno delay. I can assure this House that there is no delay. When any complaint comes to \nus, we work in collaborat ion with the Women's Commission.. We organised five \nmeetings in collaboration with them. I can assure the Member that we have very good \nterms with them and we are doing a good work. We have also written to the Embassies \nof all these countries to form a cel l to deal with this subject. My Ministry is also \nforming cells in some States. ...(Interruptions)... \nMS. SUSHILA TIRIYA: I am not asking about terms, I am asking about delays. \n...(Interruptions)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Shrimati Brinda Karat. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: There is no delay at all. \nSHRIMATI BRINDA KARAT: Sir, I have been in touch with the Minister on this. I \npersonally believe that he has displayed sensitivity and commitment to deal with the \nissue. But the problem is very large. For examp le, in just one State of Punjab, it is \nreported that about 30,000 such cases have taken place in the last two years. This is an \nestimate which has been made So, one of the basic problems in helping the women to \naccess justice is the legal framework because a crime which is a crime in India may not \nbe a crime in other countries. For example, dowry, for which reason many of the brides \nare vanishing, is not a crime in many of the countries where they are now residents. So, \nin that connection, the main recommen dation which has been made is for India to sign, \nparticularly, protocols in the Hague Commission which will enable quick extradition of \nthose who committed this crime. \nI would like to remind the Minister that on the 7th of May in this very House when a \nsimilar question was asked, he gave a categorical assurance in response to my \nsupplementary which is as follows: \n\"The Government has already decided to sign the Hague Convention. This is being \ntaken up in the Ministry of External Affairs. It is on the move. I t may be done at the \nearliest.\" Sir, this was in May, but, unfortunately, it was not done at the earliest and, till \nnow, that Convention has not been signed. According to my information, no further \nsteps have been taken. So, would the hon. Minister kindly respond as to exactly when is \nthis going to happen, and what is the timeframe by which we can expect this? \n\n8       Oral Answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: Sir, as regards the first part of the question, I agree with \nthe hon. Minister that there are a large number of such cases ...(Interruptions)... \nAN HON. MEMBER: She is not a Minister. ...(Interruptions)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Please let the hon. Minister proceed. \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: I am sorry, Sir. ...(Interruptions)... The hon. Member is, to \nan extent, right, because I have got some reports by a social group, which made a study \nin this regard. According to this report, there were 10,000 such cases a few years ago. \nThe former Canadian High Commissioner also sent a report that there are huge n umber \nof cases. So, I am not disputing this. \nThe other basic question is, it is true that I gave an assurance. On that basis, the \nMinistry of External Affairs has already moved for membership in the Hague \nConference. But one country has to sponsor it. The Government of Netherlands has \nalready sponsored it. The Government of Netherlands sponsored our application for the \nmembership. Now, the general body has to approve it. The approval has to be \nunanimous. So, our Ambassador is doing all kinds of canvassing t o see that it is \naccepted. This has already been moved and Netherlands has sponsored our case. That is \nwhere it stands today, and we will move it again. \n \nश्रीमती सुषमा स्वराज : सभाप�त महोदय, म� मंत्री महोदय से यह जानना चाहती हूं �क \nहम सब यह स्वीकार कर रहे ह� �क भारतीय कन्याओं क� प्रवासी भारतीय� से शाद� के \n�सल�सले म� धोखाधडी क� �शकायत� बढ़ती जा रह� है । ये �शकायत� सह� जानकार� के अभाव \nम� बढ़ रह� है । वहां पर ल ड़ के कमाते कम ह� और बताते  ज्यादा ह�, करते कु छ ह� और \nबताते कु छ ह� । म�  मंत्री महोदय से यह जानना चाहती हूं �क हर दे श म� हमारे �मशन्स ह�, \nअगर हमारे �मशन्स वहां रहने वाले भारतीय� के बारे म� एक सह� डाटा नैट पर उपलब्ध करवा \nद� तो यह �शकायत� अगर मुकम्मल तौर पर नह� तो 90 परस�ट जरूर समाप्त हो सकती है । \nक्या आप अपने �मशन्स को यह �नद�श जार� कर� गे �क वहां रहने वाले भारतीय� के बारे म� \nसह� और पू\nणर् जानकार� नैट पर उपलब्ध कराई जाए ?  \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: Sir, there are two ways to deal with this subject. One is, \nyes, we are in touch with the Indian Missions, and we are trying to sensitise them to \nhave the details as much as possible. When some complaint goes to them, they register \nthat complaint and inform us also. If there is a direct complaint, we write them back. \nThis is one side. The other side is, there are also some campaigns to be launched in the  \ncountry itself. We have taken some initiatives. After the Supreme Court judgement, we \nhave written to all the State Governments for compulsory registration of marriages. We \nhave made an enactment. This is number one. \nNumber two is, Sir, the awareness camp aigns will begin within one or two months. \nThere are three ways, electronic media, publication, and films, by which we are going to \nlaunch a big campaign, in collaboration with the States. Sir, we are going to involve \nStates also. These kinds of awareness campaigns will be  launched in villages also. Sir, \nthe other thing is, we are organising seminars in different States involving people, and \nwe \"want to have participation from panchayat members also. \n\nOral Answers [30 AUG, 2007] to Questions      9 \nSo, the awareness campaign is one of the most important things. ...(Interruptions)...  \nSHRIMATI BRINDA KARAT: Monitoring cells in the   ...(Interruptions).. \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Please continue Mr. Ravi. \nSHRIMATI SUSHMA SWARAJ: Sir, I am not talking about complaints. Mr. \nMinister, I am only saying that providing data should be made mandatory and \ncompulsory. \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: Madam, definitely, I will discuss this matter with the \nMinister of External Affairs. I will make it compulsory. Through them, I will proceed \non this matter. I am explaining to you what is being done in States also. We are \nrequesting the State Governments to have a cell. In every State, there should be a Cell in \nevery Department on this subject. Prosecution is one of the major things which we can \ndo. \nSir, we also want to have a provision relating to repatriation and impounding of \npassports. As for impounding of passports, it has been recommended by the National \nCommission of Women. We have referred it to the Ministry of External Affairs to know \nwhat acti on they can take. Then, photograph of wife should also be there in the \npassport. There are some difficulties. We are taking up those difficulties. Whatever \npositive suggestions have come from the National Commission of Women, and in \nwhatever way we can imp lement all this, we are discussing all these matters. We are \nexpediting it. I can only say that we don't want further delay We want to do it as early as \npossible. All these things are coming in one stroke. Much better. I hope the things will \nbe much better. \n \nश्री मोती लाल वोरा : माननीय सभाप�त जी, म� माननीय मंत्री जी से यह जानना चाहता \nहूं �क सन 2005, 2006, 2007 म� उन्ह� जो �शकायत� �मल� ह�, उन �शकायत� पर उन्ह�ने \nऎसी कौन सी कारर्वाई क� है �क िजससे सभी �शकायतकत्तार्ओं को राहत �मले? म� यह \nजानना चाहता हूं �क �कन-�कन राज्य� म� इस प्रकार क� �शकायत� बढ़ रह� ह�? जैसा�क हम \nसभी सोचते ह� �क पंजाब म� लगभग तीस से प�तीस हजार म�हलाओं को उ न के प्रवासी प�तय� \nने छोड़ रखा है, ऎसे �कतने राज्य ह�, जहां से माननीय मंत्री जी को �लखने के बाद उनका \nजवाब �मला है और जो �शकायत� माननीय मंत्री जी को, उ न के मंत्रालय को �मल� ह�, उन \nपर उन्ह�ने कौन सी कारर्वाई क� है ?  \nSHRI VAYALAR RAVI: Sir, there are a large number of complaints. I think, out of \n179 complaints, 53 are from Punjab, 33 are from Delhi; 16 are from Andhra Pradesh; 12 \nare from U.P.; 13 are from Haryana and like that. But these are only those complaints \nwhich I have received. There are other Ministries and agencies which also receive such \ncomplaints. The Ministry of Women and Child Development also receives complaints \nin large numbers. The National Commission on Women receives complaints; the \nHuman Rights Commission also receives complaints. So, they all have to be compiled \ntogether. Even various reports show this. I am not exaggerating. The report of the \nCouncil of Social Research in New Delhi a few years ago said that they suspect that the \nminimum number of such complaints would be 10,000 from Punjab alone. There is a \nCanadian report also which shows that this number is almost 20,000. \n\n10     Oral Answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nNow, with regard to the point as to what action we have taken, Sir, I would like to \nagain repeat that as soon as such complaints are received, we immediately refer them to \nthe concerned Embassies. Then we write a letter to the Chief Ministers  concerned. Then \nfollows the prosecution proceedings on the woman's complaint. So, on the one side, \nthere is the provision of prosecution, and on the other side, we see in what way we can \ndeal with them in the host countries in which they are living. Then,  there is a proposal \nwhich has yet to take place legally. Once we become a member of the Hague \nConference, the International Private Law will come into operation. On that basis, the \ntwo things, 44A of the Civil Procedure Code as well as 29C of the Civil Pr ocedure Code \nwould become applicable once we become a member, and then there will be a bilateral \nagreement with these countries. \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Next question, Q. No. 243. ...(Interruptions)... \n \nश्रीमती �वप्लव ठाकु र : सर, यह इतनी इम्पोट�न्ट बात है, हम� भी बोलने का टाइम \n�दया जाए ...(व्यवधान)... इतनी इम्पोट�न्ट बात है...(व्यवधान)... हम� टाइम �दया \nजाए...(व्यवधान)... म�हलाओं को बोलने �दया जाए...(व्यवधान)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Please. Q. No. 243. ...(Interruptions)... Q. No.. 243. \n...(Interruptions)... \nSHRIMATI B RINDA KARAT: Sir, we never get a chance. Please see how many \nMembers want to speak. ...(Interruptions)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: I understand the importance of the subject. But there are \nquestions which have to be gone through. ...(Interruptions)... There are other procedures \nby which this subject can be discussed at length. ...(Interruptions)... \nSHRI SANTOSH BAGRODIA: Sir, please allow a Half -an-Hour discussion. ... \n(Interruptions)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: The concerned Members can request for a Half -an-Hour \nDiscussion on this subject. ...(Interruptions)... Q. No. 243 please. ... (Interruptions)... \n  \nश्रीमती �वप्लव ठाकु र : इसे रख ल�िजए...(व्यवधान)... हम कर द� गे ।  \n \n   ‘न�दय� के संर�ण के �लए राष्ट्र�य – नी�त’ \n \n †*243. श्री प्यारे लाल खंडेलवाल : क्या प्रधान मंत्री यह बताने क� कृ पा कर� गे �क \n: \n \n ( क) क्या यह भी सच है �क दे श क� अ�धकांशत: बडी न�दय� का जल प्रदू�षत \nहोकर काला पड़ चुका है; \n ( ख) क्या यह भी सच है �क उक्त समस्या से �नपटने के �लए �कये गए सारे \nप्रयास �वफल रहे है; \n ( ग) य�द हां, तो क्या सरकार न�दय� को प्रदूषण से बचाने के �लए कोई राष्ट्र�य \nनी�त बनाने पर �वचार कर रह� है; और  \n ( घ) य�द नह�, तो तत्संबंधी राज्यवार ब्यौरा क्या है? \n†मू\nल सू\nचना �हन्द� म� प्राप्त हुई । \n \n\nOral Answers [30 AUG, 2007] to Questions     11 \n   \n पयार्वरण और वन मंत्रालय म� राज्य मंत्री  ( श्री नमो नारायन मीणा) : ( क) से \n(घ) एक �ववरण सभापटल पर रखा है ।  \n \n     �ववरण \n \n ( क) से ( ग) औधो�गक प्रदूषण और अन्य प्रदूषण के गैर-�बन्दु स्रोत� के अलावा \nघरे लू प्रदूषण न�दय� के प्रदूषण का मुख्य स्रोत है । अशो�धत सीवेज का अवरोधन और \n�दशाप�रवतर्न और सीवेज शोधन संयंत्र लगाना नद� संर�ण योजना म� �कए गए प्रदूषण \n�नवारण काय� के मु\nख्य घटक है । जहां तक औधो�गक प्रदूषण का संबंध है इस �दशा म� \n�कए गए प्रयास� म� उधोग �व�शष्ट ब�हस्राव मानक अ�धसू�चत करना, ब�हस्राव शोधन संयत्र� \nको स्था�पत करने को बढ़ावा दे ना और पयार्वरण संर�ण अ�ध�नयम, 1986 और जल \n(प्रदूषण �नवारण और �नयंत्रण) अ�ध�नयम, 1974 के अंतगर्त के न् द्र/राज्य प्रदूषण �नयंत्रण \nबोड� द्वारा पयार्वरण क� �नगरानी करना शा�मल है ।  \n \n गंगा कायर् योजना म� दोन� चरण� के अंतगर्त अब तक पूरे हो चुके प्रदूषण �नवारण \nकाय� से अब गंगा क� जल गुणता म� गंगा कायर् योजना से पू\nवर् क� गुणता क� तु\nलना म�, \nमु\nख्य स्थल� पर, सुधार �दखाई �दया है । यमु\nना नद� के संबंध म�, नद� जल गु\nणता म�, \n�वशेष रूप से �दल्ल� म� सीवेज शोधन �मता क� मांग और उपलब्धता के बीच भार� अंतर \nहोने के कारण और नद� म� न्यू\nनतम प्रवाह सु\n�निश्चत करने के �लए स्वच्छ जल क� \nउपलब्धता क� कमी के कारण अपे��त सु\nधार नह� हुआ है । अन्य न�दय� के संबंध म� कायर् \nपू\nरा होने के �व�भन्न चरण� म� है । \n \n \n जनसंख्या म� वृिध्द के कारण, �नरंतर बढ़ते प्रदूषण भार के साथ नद� संर�ण एक \nस�क्रय कायर् है । संर�ण नी�त क� कायर्नी�तय� क� पुनर��ा और अन्य शहर� और न�दय� क� \nपहचान करना एक सतत प्र�क्रया है । जल राज्य का �वषय होने के कारण न�दय� म� प्रवा�हत \nहोने वाले प्रदूषण को रोकने के �लए उ�चत सीवरे ज अवसंरचना का सृजन करना राज्य सरकार \nक� िजम्मेदार� है । के न् द्र सरकार पहचान �कए गए प्रदू�षत स्थल� के �लए पूंजीगत कायर् करने \nके �लए के व ल एकमुश्त अनु\nदान प्रदान क र के राज्य सरकार� के प्रयास� म� सहयोग करती है । \nराष्ट्र�य नद� संर�ण योजना सरकार का एक मु\nख्य कायर्क्रम है ।  \n \n ( घ) प्रदूषण �नवारण काय� क� अनुमो�दत लागत, �कया गया व्यय और सृिजत \nसीवेज शोधन �मता का राज्यवार ब्यौरा संलग्न �ववरण म� �दया गया है ।  \n \n     �ववरण \n \n राष्ट्र�य नद� संर�ण योजना के अंतगर्त �कया गया राज्यवार ब्यौरा  \n    (करोड़ रुपये) \nक्रम सं0 राज्य अनुमो�दत लागत �कया गया व्यय सृिजत सीवेज \nशोधन संयंत्र क� \n�मता \n(एमएलडी) \n1 2 3 4 5 \nक गंगा कायर् योजना \nचरण - 1 \n   \n1 उत्तर प्रदे श 199.95 194.46 375.09 \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \nOral Answers [30 AUG, 2007] to Questions 12      \n \n1 2 3 4 5 \n2 �बहार  57.29  52.73 122.50 \n3 पिश्चम बंगाल 188.05 186.13 371.60 \n उप  योग : 445.29 433.32 869.19 \n स्थापना और \nअनुसंधान एवं \n�वकास \n   16.75   \n कुल (जीएपी-I) 462.04 433.32 869.19 \nख राष्ट्र�य नद� \nसंर�ण योजना \n   \n1 आंध्र प्रदे श 395.11 133.87  24.46 \n2 �बहार   32.42     2.98    0.00 \n3 �दल्ल� 573.73 160.70  30.00 \n4 गुजरात   93.83   6.508 232.00 \n5 गोवा   14.10   10.92   12.50 \n6 ह�रयाणा  311.06 253.92 322.00 \n7 झारखंड    41.34      1.46     0.00 \n8 कनार्टक    72.00    52.32    40.27 \n9 के र ल    18.45      0.00      0.00 \n10 मध्य प्रदे श   101.19     68.52   144.41 \n11 महाराष्ट्र   123.17   100.94    155.00 \n12 उडीसा    72.27     37.59      33.00 \n13 पंजाब  234.58   234.08    141.20 \n14 राजस्थान     13.21        0.77        0.00 \n15 त�मलनाडु  1103.10    734.24    394.36 \n16 उत्तरांचल     85.64       16.63        4.18 \n17 उत्तर प्रदे श   924.43     472.26    445.81 \n18 सिक्कम      15.81          \n8.13 \n        \n0.00 \n19 पिश्चम बंगाल    394.65       \n155.40 \n       \n75.00 \n20 नागाल�ड       31.74           \n0.00 \n          \n0.00 \n उप-योग   4651.85      \n2547.80 \n    2055.04 \n स्थापना और \nअनुसंधान एवं \n�वकास \n    130.73   \n कुल ( राष्ट्र�य \nनद� संर�ण \nयोजना) : \n 4782.58   2547.80   2055.04 \n कुल योग  5244.62   2981.12   2924.23 \n\n(क+ख) \n \n# --> ऊपर �दए गए व्यय म� राज्य सरकार द्वारा �पछले वषर् खचर् न �कए गए \nबकाया को आगे के जाया गया भारत सरकार और राज्य सरकार के �हस्से का व्यय शा�मल है \n।  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOral Answers [30 AUG, 2007] to Questions     13 \nNational policy for protection of rivers \n†*243. SHRI PYARELAL KHANDELWAL: Will the PRIME MINISTER be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that water of most of the major rivers has become  black after \ngetting polluted; \n(b) whether it is also a fact that all efforts to deal with the said problem have proved \ninfructuous; \n(c) if so, whether Government are considering to formulate any national policy to \nprotect rivers from getting polluted; and \n(d) if not the details thereof State-wise? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT AND \nFORESTS (SHRI NAMO NARAIN MEENA): (a) to (c) Domestic sewage is the major \nsource of pollution of rivers besides industrial and other non- point sources of pollution. \nInterception and diversion of raw sewage and setting up of Sewage Treatment Plants \nhave been among the main components of pollution abatement works undertaken in the \nRiver Conservation Plan. As regards pollution by industries, efforts taken include \nnotifying industry specific effluent standards, promoting setting up of Effluent \nTreatment Plants and environmental surveillance by the Central/State Pollution Control \nBoard under Environment Protection Act 1986 and Water (Prevention and Control of \nPollution) Act, 1974. \nWith the pollution abatement works completed so far in both the phases under \nGanga Action Plan, the water quality of the river Ganga has shown improvement at \nmajor locations over its pre -GAP quality. In respect of river Yamuna, the quality of \nriver water has not shown the desired improvement owing to the large gap between the \ndemand and the availability of sewage treatment capacity particularly in Delhi, and the \nlack of availability of fresh water for ensuring minimum flow in the river. The works in \nrespect of other rivers are at different stages of completion. \nConservation of rivers is a dynamic activity with the ever increasing pollution load \ndue to increase in population. Review of the strategies of conservation policy and \nidentification of additional towns and rivers is a continuous process. Water being a State \nsubject, it is the responsibility of State Governments to create proper sewerage \ninfrastructure to prevent pollution from entering the rivers. Central Government only \n\nsupplements the efforts of the State Governments by providing one time grant for \ncapital works for identified polluted stretches. The National River Conservation Plan is \na major programme of the Government. \n(d) A statement indicating state -wise approved cost of pollution abatemen t works, \nthe expenditure incurred and the sewage treatment capacity created is given in the \nstatement. \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n14     Oral Answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nStatement \nState-wise expenditure incurred under National River Conservation Plan \n(Rupees in crores)  \nSI. \nNo. \nSTATE \nApproved \nCost- \nExpenditur\ne Incurred# \nSTP \nCapacity \nCreated(mld\n) 1 2 3 4 5 \nA \n1 \nGANGA ACTION PLAN PHASE-I \nUttar Pradesh \n199.95 194.46 375.09 \n2 Bihar 57.29 52.73 122.50 \n3 West Bengal 188.05 186.13 371.60 \n SUB TOTAL : 445.29 433.32 869.19 \n Estt. and R&D 16.75   \n TOTAL (GAP-I) : 462.04 433.32 869.19 \nB       NATIONAL RIVER CONSERVATION \nPLAN  \n1 Andhra Pradesh 395.11 133.87 24.46 \n2 Bihar 32.42 2.98 0.00 \n3 Delhi 573.73 160.70 30.00 \n4 Gujarat 93.83 95.08 232.00 \n5 Goa 14.10 10.92 12.50 \n6 Haryana 311.06 253.92 322.00 \n7 Jharkhand 41.34 1.46 0.00 \n8 K