ken up for cleaning is the river Pampa, on the bank of which is the famous \nAyyappa Temple. Sir, even though the Pampa Action Plan for cleaning the pampa river \nhad been announced a couple of years back, so far, it has not been implemented and it is \nprogressing at a snail's pace. I would like to know from the hon. Minister what is the \nreason for the inordinate delay in implementing and complet ing this Pampa Action Plan. \nWill the Minister take steps to see that the project is implemented and completed as \nearly as possible? \nSHRI NAMO NARAIN MEENA: I have got the information with regard to Pampa \nriver. We have approved certain projects of Pampa ri ver amounting to Rs. 1,845 lakhs. \nThe DPRs will be considered as and when the State Government sends them to us. I will \nlet the hon. Member know the exact position.. \nSHRI MANOHAR JOSHI: Sir, I would like to say that no doubt the problem is with \nthe State Governments. The hon. Prime Minister also mentioned. In our country, getting \nwater or pure water should be a fundamental right. Sir, I really do not understand as to \nwhat is the difficulty for the Government in making a national policy on this issue. The \nquestion was asked but the reply has not been given. Why is the Government not \ndeclaring a national policy for making available the pure water to the people? \nSHRI NAMO NARAIN MEENA: Sir, as far as this question is concerned, there is a \nNational River Conserv ation Authority under the chairmanship of the hon. Prime \nMinister, and, that is a policy formulation body. The hon. Prime Minister has asked me \nand other officers to prepare a strategy as to what should be done, how to revamp this \nentire system, and, what should be the approach. The approach should be holistic, The \nmain reason is this. Sir, for the time being we are only improving the water quality. But, \nthere is a need of quantity also. The minimum flow of river should be there. That is not \nthere in the pr esent situation. Therefore, I agree that there should be a policy. And, the \nagenda for the next meeting of the Authority will include review of river conservation \nstrategy, institutional arrangement for a holistic programme, unlocking of potential \nhuman, t echnical, financial and independent monitoring. These things are going to be \ndiscussed in the coming meeting of the Authority which is going to be held under the \nChairmanship of the hon. Prime Minister. \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Question No. 244. ...(Interruptions)...  Please, proceed with the \nQuestions. ...(Interruptions)... \nDR. MURLI MANOHAR JOSHI: Sir, it is an important question and the river \nGanga. ...(Interruptions)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Every Starred Question is an important question. \n...(Interruptions)... You can seek a discussion. ...(Interruptions)... \n \nप्रो0 राम दे व भंडार� : सर, इस पर चचार् करा द� जाए । ...(व्यवधान)... \n\n22     Oral Answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nSHRI SITARAM YECHURY: May I request you, Sir, that as the Chairman, you \nmay rule that there can be a Half-an-Hour discussion. ...(Interruptions)... \n \nप्रो0 रामदे व भंडार� : सर, इस पर half-an-hour�डस्कशन कर द�िजए \n।...(व्यवधान)... \nMR. CHAIRMAN: It is always open to Members to seek a half -an-hour discussion. \n...(Interruptions)... Please make a request. I assur e you, you will get it. \n...(Interruptions)... \nDR. MURLI MANOHAR JOSHI: You don't allow a discussion here. \n...(Interruptipons)... You don't allow me to raise a question. ...(Interruptions)... When I \nask for a Half -an-Hour discussion, you don't allow ...(Interruptions)... What does it \nmean? ...(Interruptions)... Ganga is not a State river. ...(Interruptions)... It is a national \nriver. ...(Interruptions)... One million people come.. .(Interruptions).. \nMR. CHAIRMAN: I wish ...(Interruptions)... Please sit down.  I can't hear whatever \nyou are saying ...(Interruptions)... There are five voices coming from one side. \n...(Interruptions)... I can't hear anything. ...(Inte