mir Jammu and Kashmir \n10. Jharkhand Jharkhand \n11. Karnataka Karnataka \n12. Kerala Kerala \n13. Madhya Pradesh Madhya Pradesh \n14 a) Maharashtra (excluding Mumbai) Maharashtra \n14 b) Mumbai - \n15. Meghalaya N.E.-I \n16. Mizoram N.E.-I \n17. Tripura N.E.-I \n18. Arunachal Pradesh N.E.-II \n19. Nagaland N.E.-II \n20. Manipur N.E.-II \n21. Orissa Orissa \n22. Punjab Punjab \n23. Rajasthan Rajasthan \n24. Tamil Nadu Tamil Nadu \n25. Uttaranchal Uttaranchal \n\nWritten Answers to [30 AUG., 2007] Unstarred Questions     67  \n1 2 3 \n26. Uttar Pradesh U.P. (E) & U.P. (W) \n27. West Bengal West Bengal \n28. West Bengal Kolkata District \n29. Tamil Nadu Chennai District \n30. Delhi - \nMission mode project under National Governance Plan \n1855. SHRI A. VIJAYARAGHAVAN: Will the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS  \nAND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the competent authority of Kerala has represented during J une 2007 for \napproval of the 20 mission mode project submitted by Kerala under the National \nGovernance Plan; \n(b) if so, whether the detailed project report submitted for capacity building and the \nproject report for the mission mode had been approved by the competent authority; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) if not, the reasons therefor? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (DR. SHAKEEL AHMAD): (a) Yes, Sir. DIT \n(Department of Information Technology) has received se venteen (17) Mission Mode \nprojects, out of these 11 pertain to State MMPs as approved under NeGP and 6 State \nspecific MMPs have been submitted by the Kerala Government. \n(b) to (d) The Capacity Building DPRs (Detailed Project Reports) have been \nreceived fro m various States/UTs including Kerala, and a comprehensive Capacity \nBuilding Scheme covering all States/UTs has been formulated for Human Resource and \nTraining initiatives under NeGP. This scheme is currently being processed for approval \nof the Competent A uthority. The proposal of State Government of Kerala cannot be \nconsidered at this stage since the Scheme has not been approved by the Competent \nAuthority. \nNew telephone exchanges in NER \n1856. SHRI O.T. LEPCHA: Will the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of new telephone exchanges set up in the North Eastern Region \nparticularly in Sikkim during the last three years, district-wise/year-wise; \n(b) the details of telephone exchanges to be installed in the region dur ing the \nEleventh Five Year Plan, district-wise; and \n(c) if so, the necessary steps being taken by Government in this regard? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (DR. SHAKEEL AHMAD): (a) Sir, number of new \ntelephone exchanges set up by Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL) in the,North  \n\n68     Written Answers to [RAJYA SABHA] Unstarred Questions \nEastern Region particularly in Sikkim during the last three years, District-wise/year-\nwise is given in Statement-I {See below). \n(b) Details of telephone exchanges to be installed in the Region during first year of \nthe Eleventh Five Year Plan (2007-08) is given in Statement-II {See below). \n(c) Action has been taken for procurement of equipment and preparation for \nnecessary infrastructur e in Arunachal Pradesh, Manipur and Nagaland. Material \nrequirement in Meghalaya, Mizoram and Tripura (North East -I Circle) is also being \nexamined.  \n \nStatement-I \nName of exchanges set up in the \nNorth Eastern Region during the last three years  \nSI. Name of Name of  2004-05 2005-06 2006-07 \nNo. State District  Location Location Location \n1 2 3  4 5 6 \n1 Sikkim East Sikkim  Nil Nil Sherathang \n2 Assam Bongaigaon \nGoalpara \n  Dangtol \nGoalpara \n \n  Nalbari \nDibrugarh \n Tiloi Gobradal  \n  Tinsukia \nSibsagar \nMorigaon \nNagaon \n Anandapara Makum Road \nTengapukhuri \nKijisatra \nAmbari \nSingimari \nPhuroniati \nGorajan \nBurgaon \nNaukhuti \n Cachar   Sibpur  \n     Kaptanpur  \n3 Arunachal \nPradesh \nEast Kameng    Kimi \n4 Manipur Chandel \nSepapati \nThoubal \n Chakpikarong Saitu \nGamphajol Sugnu \n  \n5 Nagaland Zunheboto \nKohima \nWokha \nDimapur \n Phugoboto \nChakabama \nChunlika \nBhandari Chukitong \nRangapahar \n6 Mizoram . Nil  Nil Nil Nil \n7 Meghalaya East Garo Hills Kharkutta   \n    Mendel   \n  East Khasi Hills Lawbah  Neighrihms \n    Forest Colony  Police Bazar \n\nWritten Answers to [30 AUG., 2007] Unstarred Questions     69  \n1       2 3 4 5 6 \n West Khasi \nHills Ri Bhoi \nJaintia Hills \nMalankona \nUmden \nLaska  \n8      Tripura South Tripura \nWest Tripura \nSalgarah \nGolaghat \nKhumwlong \nBodhjungnagar \n  \nStatement-II \nName of exchange to be installed in the North Eastern Region \nduring first year (2007-08) in the Eleventh Five Year Plan  \nSI. Name of State Name of District Locations \nNo.    \n1. Sikkim  Nil \n2 Assam  Nil \n3. Arunachal Pradesh Anjaw Hawi \n  Passighat Doloamukh \n4. Manipur Imphal West Mayang Imphal \n  Imphal East Porompat \n5. Nagaland  Nil \n6. Mizoram Lunglei Pukpui \n  Aizawl South Himen \nChaltlang \n7. Meghalaya Jaintia Hills Nongtalang \n8. Tripura West Tripura Capital Complex \nExpansion of NIC rural areas \n1857. S HRI O.T. LEPCHA: Will the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to state: \n(a) the details of National Informatics Centres (NIC) functioning at present in the \ncountry; State-wise till date; \n(b) whether Government have formulated any policy to expand it in rural areas of the \ncountry; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof indicating the functions and role of NIC? \n\n70     Written Answers to [RAJYA SABHA] Unstarred Questions \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATION AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (DR. SHAKEEL AHMAD): (a) NIC (National \nInformatics Centre) is providing backbone e -governance network (NICNET) and \ntechnical support to the Central Government Departments, States, UTs and District \nAdministrations in the country for Internet, e -mail, file transfer, database development, \ne-Governance applications development, office automation, capacity building, \nconsultancy, hosting and databases access. \nThe e-governance network and infrastructure of NIC consists of VSATs and leased \nlines upto district level comprising about 3000 nodes, Internet Data Centre at NIC Delhi \nwith storage capacity of 110 tera bytes, data centres at state capitals having storage \ncapacity from 2-5 tera bytes, video conferencing facility in state centres and at districts \nnumbering 580 locations, internet -gateway having 700 Mbps bandwidth, Certifying \nAuthority for Digital Signature in G2G domain, training facilities at NIC Hqr. and State \nGovernment Secretariats, network security, Disaster Recovery Centre at Hyderabad.  \nThe major e-governance applications implemented/supported by NIC include: \n- Passport Management System \n- Computerization of Courts \n- Property Registration System \n- Customs (Computerization \nof Customs and EDI Services) \n- PGRAMS (Public Grievance \nRedress & Monitoring System) \n- Computerized Rural Information \nSystems Project \n(i) Rural Soft (ii) Rural Bazar \n(iii) Priasoft (iv) Open eNRICH \n- National Rural Employment \nGuarantee Scheme 2005 \n- Integrated System for Rural \nDrinking Water-Computerization \n- Stamina (Sales Tax Administration \nManagement Information Network \nAided System) \n- VAT Computerization \n- Visa Issuance System \n \n- Land Records Computerization \n- Web enabled services \n- AGMARKNET (Agriculture \nMarkets Network) \n- CIPA (Common Integrated \nPolice Application) \n- National Panchayat Portal \n-Treasury Computerization \n-Web Services for the Benefits \nof Citizens \n\nWritten Answers to [30 AUG., 2007] Unstarred Questions     71  \n     -    DC*Suite -    NAIDISHA \n-    Lok Vani -    COMPACT/PAO 2000 \n-    e-Lekha -    e-Procurement \n         -    Community Information Centre (CIC)    - India Portal \nThese applications have been implemented in various States/UTs/Districts as per \ntheir priority and local requirements. More details are available on NIC Website: \nhttp://oJferings.nic.  in. \nThe functioning of NICNET in various States/Union Territories is given in \nStatement (See below). \n(b) No, Sir. \n(c) Does not arise. \nStatement \nFunctioning of NIC in the States/UTs  \nSI. Name of Total No. of Districts Remarks \nNo. State/UT Number of \nDistricts \nhaving NICNET \nconnectivity \n \n1 2 3 4 5 \n1 Andaman and \nNicobar \n3 2 1 district is newly \ncreated \n2 Andhra Pradesh 23 23 - \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 16 13 1 district is newly \ncreated. Site is not \nready for 2 districts. \n4 Assam 27 23 4 districts are newly \ncreated. \n5 Bihar 38 38 - \n6 Chandigarh 1 1 - \n7 Chhattisgarh 18 16 2 districts are newly \ncreated. \n8 Dadra and Nagar \nHaveli \n1 1 - \n9 Daman and Diu 2 2    - \n10 Delhi 9 9  _  \n\n72     Written Answers to [RAJYA SABHA] Unstarred Questions  \n1 2 3 4 5 \n11 Goa 2 2 - \n12 Gujarat 25 25 - \n13 Haryana 20 20 - \n14 Himachal Pradesh 12 12 - \n15 Jammu and \nKashmir \n22 14 8 districts are newly \ncreated. \n16 Jharkhand 22 22 - \n17 Karnataka 29 27 2 districts are newly \ncreated. \n18 Kerala 14 14 - \n19 Lakshadweep I 1 - \n20 Madhya Pradesh 48 48 - \n21 Maharashtra 35 35 - \n22 Manipur 9 9 - \n23 Meghalaya 7 7 - \n24 Mizoram 8 5 3  districts centres are \nbeing created. \n25 Nagaland 11 8 3  districts  centres are \nbeing created. \n26 Orissa 30 30 - \n27 Puducherry 4 4 - \n28 Punjab 20 17 3 districts are newly \ncreated. \n29 Rajasthan 32 32 - \n30 Sikkim 4 4  \n31 Tamil Nadu 30 30 - \n32 Tripura 4 4 - \n33 Uttar Pradesh 70 70 - \n34 Uttarakhand 13 13 - \n35 West Bengal 18 18 - \n\nWritten Answers to [30 AUG., 2007] Unstarred Questions     73 \nComputerization of post offices in Rajasthan \n†l858. DR. PRABHA THAKUR: Will the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of computers installed in the post offices in the country particularly \nin Rajasthan during the last three years, location-wise; and \n(b) the locations in the State of Rajasthan where the computers are proposed to be \ninstalled during the current year? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (DR. SHAKEEL AHMAD): (a) In the last three \nyears, the number of Computers installed in Post Offices across the country is 33027. In \nthe State of Rajasthan the number of Computers installed during the last 3 years \nlocation-wise is given in the Statement (See below). \n(b) In the current year, proposals a re being called for from the States to process \nintroduction of Computers in Post Offices. On receipt of such information and approval \nof proposal of Computerisation and Networking of Post Offices by the Planning \nCommission, the locations in the State of Ra jasthan for introducing Computers will be \nidentified and accordingly decided. \nStatement \nList of offices in Rajasthan Circle computerised during 2004-05  \nSI. \nNo. \nName of \nComputerised \nPost Office \nName of District No. of \nComputers \nsupplied \n1 2 3 4 \n1 Mayo Ajmer Aimer 4 \n2 Shastri Nagar Ajmer 4 \n3 Kesar Ganj Ajmer Aimer 4 \n4 Raj. Education Board Ajmer 4 \n5 Beawar Ajmer 10 \n6 Madanganj, Kishanganj Aimer 7 \n7 Nasirabad Ajmer 8 \n8 Bijai Nagar Ajmer 4 \n9 Kekri Ajmer 4 \n10 Ajmer Ajmer 6 \n11 Bahror Alwar 7 \n12 M.D. Alwar Alwar 10 \n13 Alwar Alwar 6 \n†Original notice of the question was received in Hindi. \n\n74     Written Answers to [RAJYA SABHA] Unstarred Questions  \n1 2 3 4 \n14 Banswara Banswara 5 \n15 Baran Baran 4 \n16 Chabra Baran 4 \n17 Banner Banner 8 \n18 Balotra, Jodhpur Banner 4 \n19 Siwana Banner 4 \n20 Chohtan Banner 4 \n21 Dhorimana Banner 4 \n22 Bharatpur Bharatpur 8 \n23 Bharatpur City Bharatpur 7 \n24 Deeg Bharatpur 7 \n25 Kaaman Bharatpur 4 \n26 Nadbai Bharatpur 4 \n27 Bayana Bharatpur 7